    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d154">

                <pb facs="0263" n="161" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg161"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A5/590: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the American Delegation</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-12-17T12:00:00+00:00">December 17,
                            1935—12 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 17—6:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>24. I am officially denying a United Press report to the effect that at today’s
                    bilateral conversations between the Japanese and ourselves, Nagano<anchor n="7"
                        xml:id="d154-f1"/> stated that Japan was bound to reject a horizontal 20%
                    reduction in naval strength because of the popular apprehension prevailing in
                    Japan regarding the possibility of a United States attack.</p>
                <p>Nagai<anchor n="8" xml:id="d154-f2"/> told me that the Japanese delegation would
                    do likewise.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d154-f1" n="7" xml:id="d154-f1-content">
                <p>Admiral Osami Nagano, Japanese delegate to the Naval Conference.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d154-f2" n="8" xml:id="d154-f2-content">
                <p>Matsuzo Nagai, Japanese Ambassador in the United Kingdom and delegate to the
                    Naval Conference.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
